      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of a natural conclusion can be so convincing, can't it? But a cliff isn't the end of the story—it's just where the author stopped writing, not where the world stops existing. You're allowed to close the book, but you're also allowed to set it down and pick up a blank page. The fog isn't the whole landscape; it's just what's in front of you right now.",
